771
00:37:15.541 --> 00:37:17.833
I'm an asshole, okay?

772
00:37:17.916 --> 00:37:20.083
It was stupid. I'm sorry.

773
00:37:20.166 --> 00:37:22.625
I'm not used to people putting me
in my place like you do.

774
00:37:22.708 --> 00:37:24.267
I don't...
Jack, I need to go to the train.

775
00:37:24.291 --> 00:37:26.017
- I need to get my...
- Let me make it up to you.

776
00:37:26.041 --> 00:37:27.333
Let me drive you to Bilbao.

777
00:37:29.916 --> 00:37:31.708
I don't want to leave things on bad terms.

778
00:37:36.875 --> 00:37:38.458
Can I drive?

779
00:37:45.541 --> 00:37:49.500
I wasted a lot of time worrying
about what other people thought of me.

780
00:37:50.083 --> 00:37:52.500
I wanted everyone to think
that I had this perfect life.

781
00:37:54.083 --> 00:37:56.833
Like, I double-majored
in economics and statistics.

782
00:37:56.916 --> 00:37:58.833
- What?
- I got a job really similar

783
00:37:58.916 --> 00:38:00.309
to the one that you're about to start.

784
00:38:00.333 --> 00:38:01.416
Really? You?

785
00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:03.583
Yes.

786
00:38:03.666 --> 00:38:06.041
And then...

787
00:38:06.125 --> 00:38:08.250
I had this health scare.

788
00:38:10.625 --> 00:38:14.250
I knew I had to make a change,
and I knew that it couldn't wait.

789
00:38:15.458 --> 00:38:19.083
So I gave up on everything
that felt like deathbed baggage.

790
00:38:20.208 --> 00:38:21.666
I know you think it's bullshit.

791
00:38:22.750 --> 00:38:25.416
The-the "trying to live
in the moment" thing.

792
00:38:25.500 --> 00:38:27.250
But it's really not to me because I...

793
00:38:27.333 --> 00:38:29.750
I wasted so much of my life.

794
00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:48.125
You got four hours
until your flight?

795
00:38:48.208 --> 00:38:51.333
Yeah, which is good
because that'll give me time

796
00:38:51.416 --> 00:38:55.000
to go through security, get settled,

797
00:38:55.083 --> 00:38:57.250
have a glass of wine or three.

798
00:38:59.458 --> 00:39:01.583
What if you didn't go in?

799
00:39:03.208 --> 00:39:04.958
Why, do you have, like, a...

800
00:39:05.041 --> 00:39:07.333
off-the-beaten-path-near-airport-adventure
for us?

801
00:39:07.416 --> 00:39:09.416
No, I'm just ask...
I'm asking what would happen

802
00:39:09.500 --> 00:39:11.625
if you didn't catch
your flight home today.

803
00:39:11.708 --> 00:39:13.434
My ticket's already booked
and paid for, Jack.

804
00:39:13.458 --> 00:39:15.000
I can't just not go.

805
00:39:15.958 --> 00:39:17.916
I can't not make it.

806
00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:21.166
My job starts in two weeks,
and I've got an apartment to move into.

807
00:39:22.250 --> 00:39:24.208
- Heather, theoretically...
- What?

808
00:39:24.291 --> 00:39:26.250
In the next four hours,

809
00:39:26.333 --> 00:39:29.333
that plane's going to leave,
and you're not on it.

810
00:39:29.416 --> 00:39:31.125
That would be really bad.

811
00:39:31.208 --> 00:39:32.791
You'd miss an apartment move-in date.

812
00:39:35.541 --> 00:39:37.416
But what happens to your life?

813
00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:38.541
Seriously.

814
00:39:45.333 --> 00:39:47.125
I've got the rest
of the money from Viktor.

815
00:39:47.208 --> 00:39:49.328
It could more than fund
a little extra time in Europe.

816
00:39:51.083 --> 00:39:52.708
Are you making plans?

817
00:39:52.791 --> 00:39:54.375
That's odd. It's very, very strange.

818
00:39:54.458 --> 00:39:56.541
It is odd. It is odd.

819
00:40:06.416 --> 00:40:07.833
Fine.

820
00:40:16.916 --> 00:40:18.541
Oh, wait.

821
00:40:19.958 --> 00:40:21.666
Oh, the girls are texting.

822
00:40:24.916 --> 00:40:26.666
Do they approve of your decision?

823
00:40:27.500 --> 00:40:29.125
Look what Amy sent.

824
00:40:34.625 --> 00:40:36.583
Yeah, they more than approve.

825
00:40:37.291 --> 00:40:39.291
Look where I am.

826
00:40:39.375 --> 00:40:41.166
Can you see? It's pretty, right?

827
00:40:41.250 --> 00:40:43.333
I need more than a text from you

828
00:40:43.416 --> 00:40:46.333
- saying that you're extending your trip.
- I know. I know. I'm sorry.

829
00:40:46.416 --> 00:40:49.083
I didn't mean to worry you
or stress you out.

830
00:40:49.166 --> 00:40:51.833
We're just having such a good time,
and it's so beautiful,

831
00:40:51.916 --> 00:40:54.000
and when else am I going
to be able to do this?

832
00:40:54.083 --> 00:40:55.500
What about your new job?

833
00:40:55.583 --> 00:40:57.463
You said you wanted
to get back and get settled.

834
00:40:57.500 --> 00:40:59.416
I mean, th-that was our plan.

835
00:40:59.500 --> 00:41:02.625
But that's why I planned for,
like, a little bit of, um...

836
00:41:02.708 --> 00:41:07.750
like a cushion in between
the vacation and when I start.

837
00:41:07.833 --> 00:41:09.625
Because, I mean, I am...

838
00:41:09.708 --> 00:41:12.791
It was because I wanted
to take some time to get settled,

839
00:41:12.875 --> 00:41:14.833
but I think... I think I'll be fine.

840
00:41:14.916 --> 00:41:16.291
I'll be back in time.

841
00:41:16.375 --> 00:41:17.976
I'm just going to come back
a little tanner.

842
00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:19.083
What about the girls?

843
00:41:20.166 --> 00:41:21.666
Uh...

844
00:41:22.541 --> 00:41:25.041
They decided
to extend their trips as well.

845
00:41:25.125 --> 00:41:26.684
Honey, I just want you
to be safe, that's it.

846
00:41:26.708 --> 00:41:28.958
I'm being safe, I promise.

847
00:41:29.041 --> 00:41:30.642
- I-I love you.
- I love you, too.

848
00:41:30.666 --> 00:41:31.791
Don't worry.

849
00:41:31.875 --> 00:41:33.583
- Okay, bye.
- Okay, bye.

850
00:41:36.041 --> 00:41:37.458
How was that?

851
00:41:38.666 --> 00:41:39.958
I feel so bad lying.

852
00:41:40.041 --> 00:41:42.333
Does he know you're traveling
around Europe with a random?

853
00:41:42.416 --> 00:41:43.833
- Hmm-mm.
- No?

854
00:41:43.916 --> 00:41:44.958
No.

855
00:41:45.541 --> 00:41:46.791
He's just worried about you.

856
00:41:46.875 --> 00:41:48.458
I know. I love him.

857
00:41:50.583 --> 00:41:53.041
I've never missed a flight before.

858
00:41:53.125 --> 00:41:54.541
Especially not on purpose.

859
00:41:54.625 --> 00:41:56.416
I'm not shocked by that.

860
00:41:57.708 --> 00:41:59.125
Look at this.

861
00:41:59.208 --> 00:42:00.416
Here.

862
00:42:02.541 --> 00:42:05.208
Yeah, "San Sebastián, 1946."

863
00:42:05.916 --> 00:42:08.083
In the heart of Donostia,

864
00:42:08.166 --> 00:42:10.666
where the sea whispers
secrets to the shore,

865
00:42:10.750 --> 00:42:15.083
"I stood on a bridge,
contemplating the end of the war."

866
00:42:17.458 --> 00:42:19.916
"One year ago,
I lay wounded on a battlefield,

867
00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:22.541
staring into the face of death.

868
00:42:23.416 --> 00:42:26.625
I don't know how or why I survived,
but I did.

869
00:42:26.708 --> 00:42:29.041
And something shifted inside me.

870
00:42:29.125 --> 00:42:33.500
I realized that my life,
however long or short, was mine alone.

871
00:42:33.583 --> 00:42:36.416
I will not waste a second of it.

872
00:42:36.500 --> 00:42:39.875
"I will not stand on the shore
and wonder what could have been."

873
00:42:43.708 --> 00:42:45.000
Come on, it's okay.

874
00:42:45.083 --> 00:42:46.184
Where are you taking me?

875
00:42:46.208 --> 00:42:48.166
It's okay. Come on.

876
00:42:48.250 --> 00:42:49.770
- I've been here before.
- Where are...

877
00:42:49.833 --> 00:42:51.958
Is this someone's house?

878
00:42:52.041 --> 00:42:54.226
Yeah. I just don't...
I don't know if anyone's home, but...

879
00:42:54.250 --> 00:42:56.041
What do you mean?

880
00:42:56.125 --> 00:42:57.750
Jack, I feel uncomfortable.

881
00:42:57.833 --> 00:42:59.142
- We can't just walk...
- It's okay.

882
00:42:59.166 --> 00:43:00.250
Trust me.

883
00:43:02.708 --> 00:43:04.541
Jack? Oh.

884
00:43:06.541 --> 00:43:07.958
Oh, my God.

885
00:43:08.041 --> 00:43:09.375
Jack!

886
00:43:09.458 --> 00:43:11.375
- Hey!
- Oi. Good to see you.

887
00:43:11.458 --> 00:43:13.125
- Good to see you.
- This is Heather.

888
00:43:13.208 --> 00:43:14.958
- Oh. Heather, nice to meet you.
- Hi. Hi.

889
00:43:15.041 --> 00:43:17.125
- I'm Ana. Ana.
- Ana. Nice to meet you.

890
00:43:18.541 --> 00:43:19.767
- Heather.
- Nice to meet you.

891
00:43:19.791 --> 00:43:20.875
Nice to meet you.

892
00:43:20.958 --> 00:43:22.101
It's been a long t...

893
00:43:22.125 --> 00:43:23.833
He knocks on the door.

894
00:43:23.916 --> 00:43:25.375
He says to us,

895
00:43:25.458 --> 00:43:28.791
"My name is Jack. I think your father knew
my great-grandfather."

896
00:43:28.875 --> 00:43:30.583
- That's it?
- No introduction.

897
00:43:30.666 --> 00:43:32.625
- No context. He just...
- He just smiled.

898
00:43:32.708 --> 00:43:33.851
Just like that.

899
00:43:33.875 --> 00:43:35.875
It's a decent smile.

900
00:43:35.958 --> 00:43:38.208
They spent hours together.

901
00:43:38.291 --> 00:43:40.333
Sometimes we translate.

902
00:43:40.416 --> 00:43:45.541
Sometimes Jack just listen to this old man
speaking a language he doesn't understand.

903
00:43:45.625 --> 00:43:48.875
I mean, at times I didn't even feel
like I needed the translation.

904
00:43:48.958 --> 00:43:51.125
- Mm.
- I didn't care. I just wanted to listen.

905
00:43:53.166 --> 00:43:54.500
Mucho. Mucho. Muchísimo.

906
00:43:54.583 --> 00:43:55.666
Muchas horas.

907
00:43:57.458 --> 00:43:58.666
- Cheers.
- Aita.

908
00:43:59.625 --> 00:44:01.250
- Heather?
- Hmm?

909
00:44:01.333 --> 00:44:03.875
Jack says, uh, you play guitar.

910
00:44:05.416 --> 00:44:06.684
- Yes, you did.
- I did?

911
00:44:06.708 --> 00:44:08.541
I'm sorry.

912
00:44:08.625 --> 00:44:10.166
- He said that.
- Jack's wrong.

913
00:44:10.250 --> 00:44:12.083
No, I believe him.

914
00:44:12.166 --> 00:44:13.750
- No, no, no, no.
- He's my friend.

915
00:44:13.833 --> 00:44:16.375
- I believe him.
- I know he's your friend, but he's wrong.

916
00:44:16.458 --> 00:44:18.083
Come on, play-play something for us.

917
00:44:18.166 --> 00:44:19.583
I don't... No. I don't...

918
00:44:19.666 --> 00:44:21.666
Yeah, play something we can all sing.

919
00:44:21.750 --> 00:44:23.041
You want to sing?

920
00:44:23.125 --> 00:44:24.208
Yes, we want to sing.

921
00:44:24.291 --> 00:44:25.875
- Okay.
- Please.

922
00:44:27.000 --> 00:44:28.480
All right.

923
00:44:29.625 --> 00:44:30.916
I'm gonna... I'll try.

924
00:44:31.000 --> 00:44:32.041
Yeah.

925
00:44:32.125 --> 00:44:35.333
But I told Jack I haven't played
since high school.

926
00:44:35.416 --> 00:44:36.750
Check it out.

927
00:44:42.250 --> 00:44:46.416
♪ Twenty-five years and my life is still ♪

928
00:44:46.500 --> 00:44:48.666
♪ trying to get up ♪

929
00:44:48.750 --> 00:44:51.958
♪ that great big hill of hope ♪

930
00:44:53.541 --> 00:44:57.375
♪ for a destination ♪

931
00:44:57.458 --> 00:44:58.791
Come on.

932
00:44:59.375 --> 00:45:03.500
♪ And so I wake in the morning
and I step outside ♪

933
00:45:03.583 --> 00:45:07.500
♪ and I take deep breath
and I get real high ♪

934
00:45:07.583 --> 00:45:13.083
♪ and I scream from the top of my lungs,
"What's going on?" ♪

935
00:45:14.333 --> 00:45:16.041
♪ And I say ♪

936
00:45:16.125 --> 00:45:20.541
♪ "Hey-ey-ey ♪

937
00:45:20.625 --> 00:45:23.458
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah" ♪

938
00:45:23.541 --> 00:45:25.625
♪ I said, "Hey! ♪"

939
00:45:27.083 --> 00:45:29.875
♪ What's going on?" ♪

940
00:45:31.708 --> 00:45:36.916
♪ And I say, "Hey-ey-ey ♪"

941
00:45:37.000 --> 00:45:39.791
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah" ♪

942
00:45:39.875 --> 00:45:42.208
♪ I said, "Hey!" ♪

943
00:45:42.291 --> 00:45:43.375
Aita.

944
00:45:43.458 --> 00:45:46.458
♪ "What's going on?" ♪♪

945
00:45:48.666 --> 00:45:51.625
That's it. That's it.

946
00:45:51.708 --> 00:45:54.083
- Good job.
- No.

947
00:46:16.416 --> 00:46:18.333
You know, I really believe that

948
00:46:18.416 --> 00:46:22.375
your thoughts help create your future.

949
00:46:25.250 --> 00:46:26.791
I'm serious.

950
00:46:26.875 --> 00:46:28.500
Sure.

951
00:46:31.250 --> 00:46:34.916
The universe, or God...

952
00:46:35.000 --> 00:46:37.208
- Mm-hmm.
- Or whatever you want to call it,

953
00:46:37.291 --> 00:46:40.666
wants for us what we want for ourselves.

954
00:46:41.333 --> 00:46:45.125
So all we have to do is think it
as often and as hard as we can.

955
00:46:48.041 --> 00:46:50.125
I don't know if I believe that.

956
00:46:52.625 --> 00:46:54.500
What do you believe?

957
00:46:55.583 --> 00:46:59.000
I'm just not sure
that the universe works like that.

958
00:46:59.083 --> 00:47:01.541
Though it'd be nice if sometimes it did.

959
00:47:50.708 --> 00:47:52.583
Where did you come from?

960
00:47:54.291 --> 00:47:55.375
Texas.

961
00:48:16.041 --> 00:48:17.541
- Hola.
- Good morning.

962
00:48:17.625 --> 00:48:19.500
- How are you doing?
- Sleepy.

963
00:48:20.583 --> 00:48:22.750
There's some breakfast over there
if you're hungry.

964
00:48:23.416 --> 00:48:25.166
It's so nice.

965
00:48:29.250 --> 00:48:32.041
How crazy there's a bath
in the master bedroom?

966
00:48:32.125 --> 00:48:34.500
- Thank you, Viktor.
- Thank you, Viktor.

967
00:48:35.666 --> 00:48:38.250
- Thank you, Russell.
- Thank you, Russell.

968
00:48:38.333 --> 00:48:40.916
It's incredible,
this whole experience, you know?

969
00:48:41.000 --> 00:48:42.000
Mm.

970
00:48:42.708 --> 00:48:45.708
I never want to stop doing it.
I just want to keep doing it forever.

971
00:48:46.750 --> 00:48:48.583
I never want it to end.

972
00:48:50.833 --> 00:48:52.541
It's very special.

973
00:48:54.375 --> 00:48:55.541
You're special.

974
00:48:59.750 --> 00:49:01.125
Can I ask you a question?

975
00:49:01.208 --> 00:49:03.041
Yes.

976
00:49:03.125 --> 00:49:05.541
If you could ask...

977
00:49:07.333 --> 00:49:11.083
God, or the universe...
here I go again...

978
00:49:11.166 --> 00:49:14.000
- Or the powers that be one question...
- Mm.

979
00:49:15.333 --> 00:49:19.708
And you get a direct answer...

980
00:49:24.041 --> 00:49:26.041
what would it be?

981
00:49:30.708 --> 00:49:32.791
What's my purpose?

982
00:49:32.875 --> 00:49:34.458
Whoa.

983
00:49:34.541 --> 00:49:36.000
Yeah.

984
00:49:37.833 --> 00:49:40.458
And I've never really
thought about that before.

985
00:49:43.166 --> 00:49:44.666
Mm.

986
00:49:50.250 --> 00:49:51.601
Do we need to dress for this?

987
00:49:51.625 --> 00:49:53.125
Yes. We have to wear

988
00:49:53.208 --> 00:49:55.666
all-white outfits and red scarves.

989
00:49:55.750 --> 00:49:57.226
You're telling me Hemingway wore that?

990
00:49:57.250 --> 00:49:59.142
- He might've.
- He's a little too cool to have worn that.

991
00:49:59.166 --> 00:50:00.958
No, you have to.

992
00:50:01.041 --> 00:50:04.875
Did you know the old bull riders,
they would drink whiskey

993
00:50:04.958 --> 00:50:07.601
until the bottle was finished,
and then they would pee in the bottle

994
00:50:07.625 --> 00:50:09.375
and drink their own pee
and pass it around?

995
00:50:09.458 --> 00:50:10.708
- What?
- Yeah.

996
00:50:10.791 --> 00:50:12.059
Do you think they still do that?

997
00:50:12.083 --> 00:50:13.291
I think they do still do it.

998
00:50:13.375 --> 00:50:17.500
That's probably why that-that
Spanish rider in The Sun Also Rises...

999
00:50:17.583 --> 00:50:19.017
Remember how he's always drinking whiskey?

1000
00:50:19.041 --> 00:50:21.708
He's drinking
his own piss for sure.

1001
00:50:21.791 --> 00:50:22.875
Potentially.

1002
00:50:41.500 --> 00:50:42.666
Wow.

1003
00:50:42.750 --> 00:50:44.291
Here we go. Here we...

1004
00:50:47.583 --> 00:50:48.903
I think they're coming through...

1005
00:50:54.083 --> 00:50:55.333
- I'm going out there.
- No.

1006
00:50:55.416 --> 00:50:56.851
- I'm going, I'm going.
- No, no, no, no.

1007
00:50:56.875 --> 00:50:58.101
- Wish me luck.
- No, no, no, no, no.

1008
00:50:58.125 --> 00:50:59.750
Jack!

1009
00:51:05.500 --> 00:51:06.833
Jack!

1010
00:51:10.500 --> 00:51:12.291
That was really stupid.

1011
00:51:14.041 --> 00:51:15.500
Stop.

1012
00:51:15.583 --> 00:51:18.666
Mm, very Hemingway-esque,
bullshit, macho thing for you to do.

1013
00:51:18.750 --> 00:51:20.291
Stop. Stop, stop, stop. Seriously.

1014
00:51:20.375 --> 00:51:21.517
I'm sorry.

1015
00:51:21.541 --> 00:51:22.958
- Don't make me laugh.
- Seriously.

1016
00:51:23.041 --> 00:51:24.083
Bien.

1017
00:51:24.166 --> 00:51:26.000
Ay.

1018
00:51:26.083 --> 00:51:28.083
I think I dislocated my shoulder.

1019
00:51:28.166 --> 00:51:29.208
Whoa.

1020
00:51:29.291 --> 00:51:31.041
Let's see what is happening, okay?

1021
00:51:31.916 --> 00:51:33.833
Do you need help? Can I help you?

1022
00:51:33.916 --> 00:51:35.333
Got it.

1023
00:51:35.416 --> 00:51:37.750
I feel like the universe is
telling you something

1024
00:51:37.833 --> 00:51:39.750
about using money that's been stolen.

1025
00:51:39.833 --> 00:51:41.976
