- Can I?

1103
00:56:31.625 --> 00:56:33.416
- Yeah. No.
- Do you mind?

1104
00:56:33.500 --> 00:56:35.875
- Look.
- Whoa.

1105
00:56:35.958 --> 00:56:38.291
No way.

1106
00:56:41.916 --> 00:56:44.708
- That is crazy.
- That's crazy.

1107
00:56:44.791 --> 00:56:46.125
Do they look familiar?

1108
00:56:46.208 --> 00:56:47.333
No, I haven't seen these.

1109
00:56:48.833 --> 00:56:51.750
"Santa Pau is a tiny village
in the Pyrenees,

1110
00:56:51.833 --> 00:56:53.708
exactly where three countries meet.

1111
00:56:53.791 --> 00:56:57.416
If you take the wrong path, you can
miss it and regret it all your life.

1112
00:56:57.500 --> 00:57:00.583
I'm here, in April,
for their festival season.

1113
00:57:00.666 --> 00:57:04.125
They're finishing the winter and welcoming
the Santa de la Primavera,

1114
00:57:04.208 --> 00:57:05.625
"the Saint of Spring."

1115
00:57:10.000 --> 00:57:13.125
"I've been here for six days,
and they have not stopped dancing."

1116
00:57:13.208 --> 00:57:15.458
They've done this for centuries.

1117
00:57:15.541 --> 00:57:18.166
They have kept the faith
that spring will come.

1118
00:57:18.250 --> 00:57:19.666
That life will go on.

1119
00:57:19.750 --> 00:57:21.458
They are dancing in the face of death.

1120
00:57:23.041 --> 00:57:24.875
Don't know when they'll stop.

1121
00:57:24.958 --> 00:57:26.750
"Maybe I won't, either."

1122
00:57:27.833 --> 00:57:30.125
- Do you think that festival still exists?
- I don't know.

1123
00:57:30.208 --> 00:57:32.750
Where is it? Santa Pau?

1124
00:57:32.833 --> 00:57:34.291
I don't know.

1125
00:57:43.125 --> 00:57:45.791
Okay, let's keep these safe.

1126
00:57:45.875 --> 00:57:47.833
You can have it.

1127
00:57:48.541 --> 00:57:49.791
Keep it.

1128
00:57:49.875 --> 00:57:51.750
