1129
00:57:55.416 --> 00:57:56.750
I love you.

1130
00:58:00.291 --> 00:58:02.375
Me, too.
I just didn't want to say it first.

1131
00:58:04.625 --> 00:58:05.875
Hi.

1132
00:58:06.583 --> 00:58:07.750
Look.

1133
00:58:08.791 --> 00:58:11.916
If you can see past that tower
over there, that's the Colosseum.

1134
00:58:12.000 --> 00:58:13.500
Do you need anything from me?

1135
00:58:13.583 --> 00:58:15.500
- You, uh, you got your flight booked?
- Mm-hmm.

1136
00:58:15.583 --> 00:58:20.375
Just enough time
to get settled into the new place and...

1137
00:58:20.458 --> 00:58:22.916
start the new job on the following Monday.

1138
00:58:23.000 --> 00:58:25.375
Okay, well,
you know you have less than a week.

1139
00:58:25.458 --> 00:58:30.750
I also wanted to call and tell you...

1140
00:58:30.833 --> 00:58:32.250
I met someone.

1141
00:58:32.333 --> 00:58:33.708
You met someone?

1142
00:58:33.791 --> 00:58:36.041
What's his name? Wh-Where is he from?

1143
00:58:36.125 --> 00:58:37.625
His name's Jack.

1144
00:58:37.708 --> 00:58:39.041
He's from New Zealand.

1145
00:58:39.125 --> 00:58:41.041
- What's he do?
- Uh...

1146
00:58:41.125 --> 00:58:43.250
Well, for a while, he's been...

1147
00:58:43.333 --> 00:58:46.708
following his great-grandfather's journal
around Europe.

1148
00:58:46.791 --> 00:58:48.833
Following a journal? Why?

1149
00:58:48.916 --> 00:58:54.000
Uh, well, his... great-grandfather was

1150
00:58:54.083 --> 00:58:58.833
a soldier in World War II,
and to honor his memory,

1151
00:58:58.916 --> 00:59:01.000
Jack is following in his footsteps.

1152
00:59:01.083 --> 00:59:03.333
It's a really beautiful story,
and I don't know,

1153
00:59:03.416 --> 00:59:05.750
maybe he'll write a book about it or...

1154
00:59:05.833 --> 00:59:06.916
Heather.

1155
00:59:07.000 --> 00:59:08.226
- I have to go.
- I love you.

1156
00:59:08.250 --> 00:59:09.250
- Bye.
- Bye.

1157
00:59:10.083 --> 00:59:11.208
Long walk.

1158
00:59:11.291 --> 00:59:12.833
- Yeah, I got lost.
- Yeah?

1159
00:59:16.250 --> 00:59:18.458
So, apparently, I'm going to write a book?

1160
00:59:22.291 --> 00:59:24.291
I, um...

1161
00:59:24.375 --> 00:59:26.000
I was going to mention it to you.

1162
00:59:26.083 --> 00:59:27.250
- Oh, yeah?
- Yeah.

1163
00:59:27.333 --> 00:59:29.250
I thought that...

1164
00:59:31.416 --> 00:59:34.250
It would give what I'm doing
some kind of a meaning?

1165
00:59:34.333 --> 00:59:36.333
No. What you're doing does have meaning.

1166
00:59:36.416 --> 00:59:40.333
I was just saying that
it's such a beautiful experience

1167
00:59:40.416 --> 00:59:42.708
and thing that you're doing.

1168
00:59:42.791 --> 00:59:45.125
It's just not really something
that I need.

1169
00:59:50.000 --> 00:59:51.291
Okay.

1170
00:59:52.500 --> 00:59:53.750
What do you need?

1171
00:59:53.833 --> 00:59:56.000
I don't need anything.

1172
00:59:57.000 --> 00:59:58.416
I've got it all right here.

1173
00:59:58.500 --> 01:00:00.833
Okay, but you know right here
is about to end, then.

1174
01:00:01.750 --> 01:00:06.166
I'm getting on a plane to New York,
and we haven't really talked about...

1175
01:00:06.250 --> 01:00:08.333
how you feel about that or what you think.

1176
01:00:08.416 --> 01:00:12.291
I think we should make the most
of every one of those days until you go.

1177
01:00:12.375 --> 01:00:13.791
Until I go, and then what?

1178
01:00:13.875 --> 01:00:15.833
- I don't know.
- You don't know?

1179
01:00:15.916 --> 01:00:17.500
I get it. You don't make plans.

1180
01:00:17.583 --> 01:00:23.041
You get distant any time I show
any sort of interest in my future.

1181
01:00:23.125 --> 01:00:25.166
But then you make these grand statements

1182
01:00:25.250 --> 01:00:29.916
about how the universe conspires
to give us what we want and what we need.

1183
01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:34.166
Why every single time I bring up anything
about the future, you get distant?

1184
01:00:34.250 --> 01:00:36.142
Because there's no point
talking about the future.

1185
01:00:36.166 --> 01:00:37.851
- There's no point talking about the...
- What do you mean

1186
01:00:37.875 --> 01:00:39.267
there's no point talking about the future?

1187
01:00:39.291 --> 01:00:40.684
What is this about, your career or...?

1188
01:00:40.708 --> 01:00:42.125
No, it-it's about all of it.

1189
01:00:42.208 --> 01:00:44.708
It's about what we're doing
moving forward.

1190
01:00:44.791 --> 01:00:47.750
I just, like, I-I'm sorry
the story thing bothered you,

1191
01:00:47.833 --> 01:00:49.875
but, like, what am I supposed to say
to my dad?

1192
01:00:49.958 --> 01:00:52.875
He's a man who's worked every single day
since he was 16 years old.

1193
01:00:52.958 --> 01:00:55.500
And he's asking me about a young man

1194
01:00:55.583 --> 01:00:57.916
wandering through Europe
following a journal.

1195
01:00:58.000 --> 01:00:59.726
I just made up a story
about you writing a book

1196
01:00:59.750 --> 01:01:01.750
because it sounds
a hell of a lot better than,

1197
01:01:01.833 --> 01:01:05.625
"I don't know, Dad, he's some
mysterious guy that I met on the train

1198
01:01:05.708 --> 01:01:10.708
who wears a $10,000 watch
and thinks that work is for squares."

1199
01:01:10.791 --> 01:01:14.083
I got this on the side of the road
for ten bucks the day that I quit my job.

1200
01:01:14.166 --> 01:01:16.642
And I keep it 'cause it reminds me
of what's real and what's bullshit.

1201
01:01:16.666 --> 01:01:20.708
Okay, so what I'm asking you,
is this real or is this bullshit?

1202
01:01:20.791 --> 01:01:22.958
Of course this is real.
Don't be ridiculous.

1203
01:01:23.041 --> 01:01:24.976
I'm just asking you a question,
and you keep deflecting.

1204
01:01:25.000 --> 01:01:26.184
What do you want me to say, Heather?

1205
01:01:26.208 --> 01:01:30.083
Maybe, I don't know, "It's killing me
that our time here is coming to an end

1206
01:01:30.166 --> 01:01:33.583
and we should make a plan
to see each other as soon as possible

1207
01:01:33.666 --> 01:01:36.708
because the thought of not seeing you

1208
01:01:36.791 --> 01:01:39.875
or being a continent away from you
is unbearable."

1209
01:01:40.916 --> 01:01:43.041
Or is that just me?

1210
01:01:45.041 --> 01:01:48.083
Heather, I... I don't know what's going
to happen in the future.

1211
01:01:48.166 --> 01:01:49.726
- I know, but...
- And I'm okay with that.

1212
01:01:49.750 --> 01:01:51.101
I-I know, but I'm not a trap, Jack.

1213
01:01:51.125 --> 01:01:53.351
I'm not some, like...
I'm not a dead end that you need to avoid.

1214
01:01:53.375 --> 01:01:55.976
- I've never lied to you about anything.
- I'm not saying that you have.

1215
01:01:56.000 --> 01:01:57.392
- But I've told you...
- That's not what I said.

1216
01:01:57.416 --> 01:01:59.684
Heather, I've told you from day one
that I don't live in the future

1217
01:01:59.708 --> 01:02:01.625
and I prefer not making big plans.

1218
01:02:01.708 --> 01:02:04.083
I know, but I-I do.

1219
01:02:04.166 --> 01:02:06.416
I like plans. I need them.

1220
01:02:06.500 --> 01:02:10.750
And I just feel like a guy
who has no plans or nowhere to be

1221
01:02:10.833 --> 01:02:13.583
could at least make one
or-or get on the plane with me.

1222
01:02:13.666 --> 01:02:15.250
I can't give you an answer right now.

1223
01:02:15.333 --> 01:02:16.601
- Come with me.
- I can't... I don't...

1224
01:02:16.625 --> 01:02:19.791
I don't know
what to tell you, Heather.

1225
01:02:20.875 --> 01:02:23.434
- And I can't have this conversation.
- You're not telling me anything right now.

1226
01:02:23.458 --> 01:02:26.041
Exactly. I can't have this conversation
with you right now.

1227
01:02:26.125 --> 01:02:28.041
Jack.

1228
01:02:28.125 --> 01:02:29.976
Jack, what do you mean
you can't have this conversation?

1229
01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:31.726
- I'm going for a walk.
- Where are you going?

1230
01:02:31.750 --> 01:02:32.750
I'm going for a walk.

1231
01:02:37.958 --> 01:02:40.166
You believe in heaven and hell?

1232
01:02:41.166 --> 01:02:44.333
I don't think I believe
in a heaven or hell.

1233
01:02:46.875 --> 01:02:49.833
I like to believe that...

1234
01:02:49.916 --> 01:02:52.041
this isn't all that we have.

1235
01:02:52.125 --> 01:02:54.666
- Yeah.
- This very, very short life.

1236
01:02:56.250 --> 01:02:58.559
I think that's the beautiful part
about it, is it's a choice.

1237
01:02:58.583 --> 01:03:01.875
We get to, we get to decide
who we're becoming every moment.

1238
01:03:02.666 --> 01:03:06.541
And it's not up to us to decide
which moment is perfect

1239
01:03:06.625 --> 01:03:08.875
and which moment isn't perfect.

1240
01:03:10.625 --> 01:03:14.708
Some of the most beautiful things come
from the most devastating losses.

1241
01:03:17.916 --> 01:03:19.791
Doesn't mean that it's not hard, though.

1242
01:03:21.250 --> 01:03:23.583
Do you believe in past lives?

1243
01:03:24.791 --> 01:03:26.750
Yes.

1244
01:03:26.833 --> 01:03:28.708
One hundred percent, yes.

1245
01:03:28.791 --> 01:03:31.208
Do you think we've met before?

1246
01:03:31.291 --> 01:03:33.541
Yeah, one hundred percent.

1247
01:03:35.916 --> 01:03:38.250
I'm starting to not...

1248
01:03:39.083 --> 01:03:41.375
believe in coincidences.

1249
01:04:01.291 --> 01:04:03.041
I'm coming with you.

1250
01:04:05.291 --> 01:04:06.875
I bought a plane ticket.

1251
01:04:15.583 --> 01:04:18.666
"They were digging in soil
that had been dug before them",

1252
01:04:18.750 --> 01:04:20.458
that will be dug after them.

1253
01:04:20.541 --> 01:04:23.500
These trees will grow, these men will die,

1254
01:04:23.583 --> 01:04:26.791
their children will harvest
these olives for their own one day.

1255
01:04:26.875 --> 01:04:30.083
We planted 19 trees
before the sun went down.

1256
01:04:30.166 --> 01:04:32.875
Whatever happens to me,
I am in their soil.

1257
01:04:32.958 --> 01:04:35.333
"I am in their grandchildren's story."

1258
01:04:35.416 --> 01:04:37.708
Is this the olive grove
Russell helped plant?

1259
01:04:37.791 --> 01:04:40.291
I don't know. It could be.

1260
01:04:42.208 --> 01:04:46.208
Potentially, we could come back
to this tree in another life.

1261
01:04:48.958 --> 01:04:51.078
Okay. What can I say?

1262
01:04:53.000 --> 01:04:54.416
It's so cute.

1263
01:04:55.500 --> 01:04:57.625
Give me your phone. Gonna take a photo.

1264
01:04:57.708 --> 01:04:59.000
You're going to do what?

1265
01:04:59.083 --> 01:05:00.333
Don't get too excited.

1266
01:05:04.083 --> 01:05:05.375
Okay, we have eight seconds.

1267
01:05:05.458 --> 01:05:06.708
What do we do? What do we do?

1268
01:05:06.791 --> 01:05:08.142
What do... what do we...

1269
01:05:19.958 --> 01:05:22.017
What?

1270
01:05:22.041 --> 01:05:23.750
Have all items
out of your pockets.

1271
01:05:26.291 --> 01:05:28.250
Keys, telephones.

1272
01:05:28.333 --> 01:05:29.958
Next.

1273
01:05:35.875 --> 01:05:38.958
This is
Dr. Donato from the Rome oncology clinic.

1274
01:05:39.041 --> 01:05:41.166
Your test results came in.

1275
01:05:41.250 --> 01:05:44.583
I think you should call me
as soon as possible, please.

1276
01:05:53.916 --> 01:05:55.250
Jack!

1277
01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:01.625
What are you doing?

1278
01:06:03.125 --> 01:06:05.333
- Should we get coffee?
- Hey, silly. Yes.

1279
01:06:17.583 --> 01:06:20.463
We will begin boarding
passengers that need assistance…

1280
01:06:20.541 --> 01:06:21.958
I'm going to go to the bathroom.

1281
01:06:22.041 --> 01:06:23.250
Okay.

1282
01:06:23.333 --> 01:06:26.416
Um... we're group five,

1283
01:06:26.500 --> 01:06:28.166
so you have a little bit of time.

1284
01:06:28.250 --> 01:06:29.333
Yeah.

1285
01:06:29.416 --> 01:06:30.958
Do you want to leave your stuff?

1286
01:06:31.041 --> 01:06:32.958
It's okay. I'm used to the weight.

1287
01:06:33.041 --> 01:06:34.125
Okay.

1288
01:06:35.208 --> 01:06:36.541
That was a really good trip.

1289
01:06:36.625 --> 01:06:39.083
Yeah, it was.

1290
01:06:39.166 --> 01:06:41.625
Every single part of it was great.

1291
01:06:43.166 --> 01:06:45.208
- Right?
- The best.

1292
01:06:47.166 --> 01:06:48.875
So good.

1293
01:06:50.875 --> 01:06:53.875
There's still so much more
I want to see, though.

1294
01:06:55.166 --> 01:06:57.291
Then we can come back.

1295
01:06:58.750 --> 01:07:00.166
Yeah.

1296
01:07:01.833 --> 01:07:04.125
Do you always get like this
when you have to pee?

1297
01:07:07.208 --> 01:07:09.666
Go pee. Hurry. Hurry back.

1298
01:07:09.750 --> 01:07:11.666
- Okay.
- Okay?

1299
01:07:15.958 --> 01:07:19.833
Passengers seated
in zone one can begin boarding.

1300
01:07:36.000 --> 01:07:38.000
New York JFK.

1301
01:07:40.875 --> 01:07:45.708
Continuing boarding
Flight 2463 to New York JFK.

1302
01:07:45.791 --> 01:07:48.833
Those seated in zone two can now board.

1303
01:08:05.208 --> 01:08:07.541
Zone three can now board.

1304
01:08:21.208 --> 01:08:23.458
New York JFK.

1305
01:08:23.541 --> 01:08:26.125
- All passengers...
- Jack!

1306
01:08:26.208 --> 01:08:28.458
Jack!

1307
01:08:28.541 --> 01:08:30.041
Hi, sir.

1308
01:08:30.125 --> 01:08:32.041
I-I'm looking for my boyfriend.

1309
01:08:32.125 --> 01:08:34.000
- No.
- Sì...

1310
01:08:35.666 --> 01:08:36.946
- Uh, but he, he...
- No, no, no.

1311
01:08:38.083 --> 01:08:39.416
Shit.

1312
01:08:39.500 --> 01:08:41.083
Oh, I'm so sorry.

1313
01:08:41.166 --> 01:08:42.458
Okay.

1314
01:08:45.500 --> 01:08:47.250
Uh, sorry.

1315
01:08:47.333 --> 01:08:48.833
Sorry.

1316
01:08:54.041 --> 01:08:59.250
Final call
for Flight 2463 to New York JFK.

1317
01:08:59.333 --> 01:09:01.267
All passengers should be in line,

1318
01:09:01.291 --> 01:09:04.041
as we will be closing
the cabin doors shortly.

1319
01:09:14.875 --> 01:09:16.375
- Hi.
- Hi.

1320
01:09:16.458 --> 01:09:20.916
Hey, um, I'm-I'm traveling with someone,
and I can't find him,

1321
01:09:21.000 --> 01:09:24.208
and I was wondering if you could tell me
if he's gotten on the plane yet.

1322
01:09:24.291 --> 01:09:26.083
I'm sorry. We're about to close the door,

1323
01:09:26.166 --> 01:09:28.791
so you need to board now
and see if they're on the plane.

1324
01:09:28.875 --> 01:09:30.892
I understand.
I was just wondering if you could tell me

1325
01:09:30.916 --> 01:09:32.958
if the person who's sitting
next to me has boarded.

1326
01:09:33.041 --> 01:09:34.666
Passport and ticket, please.

1327
01:09:41.375 --> 01:09:42.875
Thank you.

1328
01:09:45.041 --> 01:09:46.708
Okay. Buon viaggio.

1329
01:09:46.791 --> 01:09:48.208
Is it a full flight?

1330
01:09:48.291 --> 01:09:50.250
- Yes.
- Okay.

1331
01:11:29.625 --> 01:11:32.351
Another holiday
attraction opening in the city today

1332
01:11:32.375 --> 01:11:35.625
is three weeks of special events
in the Flatiron District,

1333
01:11:35.708 --> 01:11:38.083
kicking off with a pretty cool
art installation.

1334
01:11:41.208 --> 01:11:42.375
Hi!

1335
01:11:42.458 --> 01:11:43.750
Hi, hi, hi!

1336
01:11:47.500 --> 01:11:49.000
Hey, honey.

1337
01:11:50.875 --> 01:11:53.315
Wait, no, I don't...
You haven't heard, like, a word from him?

1338
01:11:53.375 --> 01:11:54.500
Nothing.

1339
01:11:54.583 --> 01:11:55.666
- Nothing?
- Nothing?

1340
01:11:55.750 --> 01:11:58.125
Nothing. Not since "I'm really sorry."

1341
01:11:58.208 --> 01:12:00.541
And then, I'm pretty sure blocking me.

1342
01:12:00.625 --> 01:12:02.208
- No.
- Yeah, the last...

1343
01:12:02.291 --> 01:12:03.291
He's literally a piece of

1344
01:12:03.375 --> 01:12:04.559
- steaming wet dog shit.
- Amy...

1345
01:12:04.583 --> 01:12:06.059
- I'm so sorry. No. No.
- Wait. No, no, no.

1346
01:12:06.083 --> 01:12:07.809
No, hold on. I'm telling you.

1347
01:12:07.833 --> 01:12:09.750
- After, after...
- Let her speak.

1348
01:12:09.833 --> 01:12:12.625
He said, "I'm really sorry,"
my message didn't go through.

1349
01:12:12.708 --> 01:12:14.668
- He blocked me.
- So he completely ghosts you

1350
01:12:14.750 --> 01:12:17.458
after going on, like, this whirlwind trip,

1351
01:12:17.541 --> 01:12:20.500
and then he tells you that he loves you,
and then he just, like,

1352
01:12:20.583 --> 01:12:22.708
straight up ghosts you
and disappears forever?

1353
01:12:22.791 --> 01:12:23.958
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

1354
01:12:24.041 --> 01:12:27.291
Mr. Jack can take his dumb accent
and his moody attitude

1355
01:12:27.375 --> 01:12:29.684
and he can just go rot in whatever
European hole he crawled out of.

1356
01:12:29.708 --> 01:12:30.708
I'm sorry. I'm over it.

1357
01:12:30.791 --> 01:12:32.726
- You deserve a thousand percent better.
- So embarrassing.

1358
01:12:32.750 --> 01:12:34.267
- No.
- No, it's not embarrassing.

1359
01:12:34.291 --> 01:12:35.559
- It's just rude.
- It's not embarrassing.

1360
01:12:35.583 --> 01:12:36.666
I just agree with her

1361
01:12:36.750 --> 01:12:39.017
- that you deserve better.
- Thank you. You deserve better.

1362
01:12:39.041 --> 01:12:40.833
I guess of all things,
I'm just so confused.

1363
01:12:40.916 --> 01:12:42.541
Like, why didn't he say something?

1364
01:12:42.625 --> 01:12:44.916
- Like, literally anything?
- Why did he... Right.

1365
01:12:45.000 --> 01:12:46.517
- Raef hasn't heard anything, either.
- What?

1366
01:12:46.541 --> 01:12:48.434
- Nothing at all. Isn't that weird?
- Really?

1367
01:12:48.458 --> 01:12:50.916
- Nothing from Jack? Since when?
- Nothing at all.

1368
01:12:51.000 --> 01:12:53.291
He says that it's real...
For a whole month, no contact,

1369
01:12:53.375 --> 01:12:55.000
and that's really unusual for Jack.

1370
01:12:55.083 --> 01:12:56.416
Hey, guys.

1371
01:12:57.000 --> 01:12:59.375
What if he is in witness protection?

1372
01:12:59.458 --> 01:13:01.250
- Amy?
- No, I'm serious.

1373
01:13:01.333 --> 01:13:02.958
What if he, like, arrived to the airport

1374
01:13:03.041 --> 01:13:05.500
and he saw his, like,
old mob boss or something,

1375
01:13:05.583 --> 01:13:07.601
and then he was like,
"Oh, my gosh, I'm going to get caught."

1376
01:13:07.625 --> 01:13:10.208
So he had to change his entire life
and identity

1377
01:13:10.291 --> 01:13:11.517
- in witness protection.
- Mm.

1378
01:13:11.541 --> 01:13:13.309
That would make sense
why he, like, went no contact.

1379
01:13:13.333 --> 01:13:14.559
- It's definitely...
- Duh.

1380
01:13:14.583 --> 01:13:17.392
No, it's a way better story than
"I got ghosted by a guy I met in Europe."

1381
01:13:17.416 --> 01:13:20.208
No, I really, I really think so,
because he wasn't...

1382
01:13:20.291 --> 01:13:22.267
He wouldn't be... I mean, let's be honest,
he would not be good in the mob.

1383
01:13:22.291 --> 01:13:23.291
No.

1384
01:13:23.375 --> 01:13:25.916
The only reason he would be
is because he's bad at pictures.

1385
01:13:26.000 --> 01:13:28.083
Wait.

1386
01:13:28.166 --> 01:13:30.125
- This is adding up.
- It's...

1387
01:13:30.208 --> 01:13:31.625
It's adding up, and then...

1388
01:13:31.708 --> 01:13:32.934
Actually, keep it coming, keep it coming.

1389
01:13:32.958 --> 01:13:34.142
I think you're on to something.

1390
01:13:34.166 --> 01:13:38.250
He was in the mob, he wasn't good at it,
and so then he had to quit the mob,

1391
01:13:38.333 --> 01:13:40.458
and then he had to go
into witness protection.

1392
01:13:40.541 --> 01:13:42.250
Feeding my delusions.

1393
01:13:42.333 --> 01:13:44.601
- That's what I'm here for.
- I love it. I love your brain.

1394
01:13:44.625 --> 01:13:46.041
Thank you. I love it, too.

1395
01:13:49.791 --> 01:13:51.416
It's a holiday next week,

1396
01:13:51.500 --> 01:13:54.250
so... let's jump into it.

1397
01:13:54.333 --> 01:13:57.750
Um, I think everything,
everything is looking pretty good.

1398
01:13:57.833 --> 01:14:00.708
One note on page…

1399
01:14:19.208 --> 01:14:20.625
Merry Christmas from Texas.

1400
01:14:20.708 --> 01:14:22.166
I just got home.

1401
01:14:22.250 --> 01:14:23.916
Um, family's good.

1402
01:14:24.500 --> 01:14:26.333
- Hey, there she is.
- Hi. Hi.

1403
01:14:28.250 --> 01:14:29.416
- Hi, Nana.
- Oh, oh.

1404
01:14:29.500 --> 01:14:31.333
- How are you?
- Oh, you're all skin and bone.

1405
01:14:31.416 --> 01:14:33.583
Uh, Dad says hi.

1406
01:14:33.666 --> 01:14:34.916
Nana says hi.

1407
01:14:35.000 --> 01:14:36.416
Come on, let me at her.

1408
01:14:37.791 --> 01:14:38.791
Mm!

1409
01:14:38.875 --> 01:14:41.017
- I missed you so much.
- Oh, let me get a look at you.

1410
01:14:41.041 --> 01:14:42.934
- Oh, come on, help me get this ham on.
- All right.

1411
01:14:42.958 --> 01:14:44.558
Can't make my Christmas ham without you.

1412
01:14:44.625 --> 01:14:45.708
Absolutely not.

1413
01:14:45.791 --> 01:14:47.916
- You got a beer?
- Oh, hell yeah, I got a beer.

1414
01:14:48.000 --> 01:14:50.875
Uh, yeah, I love y'all. Merry Christmas.

1415
01:14:54.583 --> 01:14:55.583
Hey.

1416
01:14:57.083 --> 01:14:58.375
What's eating you?

1417
01:15:00.083 --> 01:15:02.208
When Mom left,

1418
01:15:02.291 --> 01:15:04.708
how did...

1419
01:15:04.791 --> 01:15:07.041
How did you cope?

1420
01:15:07.125 --> 01:15:09.458
Well, I had to know it wasn't about me.

1421
01:15:09.541 --> 01:15:11.416
And it wasn't about you.

1422
01:15:11.500 --> 01:15:13.541
I mean, look at us.

1423
01:15:13.625 --> 01:15:16.166
We're cuter than two peas in a pod.

1424
01:15:25.958 --> 01:15:28.500
I could never be inside your mom's brain.

1425
01:15:28.583 --> 01:15:30.083
Hmm.

1426
01:15:30.166 --> 01:15:32.791
I could hate her...

1427
01:15:32.875 --> 01:15:35.416
for leaving us, for leaving you.

1428
01:15:35.500 --> 01:15:39.166
Well, I could love her
for-for giving you to me.

1429
01:15:40.125 --> 01:15:44.708
For giving me this one-on-one relationship
with the best girl in the whole world.

1430
01:15:45.625 --> 01:15:48.125
But trust me, baby,
I, uh, I spent a lot of years,

1431
01:15:48.208 --> 01:15:51.708
I-I wasted a lot of years
on the hate part.

1432
01:15:52.791 --> 01:15:54.666
Same.

1433
01:15:54.750 --> 01:15:57.250
Oh, Heather, baby, honey.

1434
01:15:58.250 --> 01:16:00.333
You got a great life.

1435
01:16:00.416 --> 01:16:02.666
You got a life better
than I ever even dreamed of.

1436
01:16:02.750 --> 01:16:04.375
You got a great education.

1437
01:16:04.458 --> 01:16:05.708
You got a, a great job.

1438
01:16:05.791 --> 01:16:07.416
You got a great future.

1439
01:16:08.000 --> 01:16:11.041
You do not let this boy
take that away from you.

1440
01:16:11.875 --> 01:16:13.083
You hear me?

1441
01:16:13.166 --> 01:16:14.500
He won't.

1442
01:16:16.125 --> 01:16:17.875
He doesn't get to do that.

1443
01:16:21.750 --> 01:16:24.666
I'm going to help Nana put the greens on.

1444
01:16:28.666 --> 01:16:31.333
Wait, your room's so cutie.

1445
01:16:31.416 --> 01:16:34.083
Wait, look how crazy Connie looks

1446
01:16:34.166 --> 01:16:35.625
- in that photo.
- Look at Connie.

1447
01:16:35.708 --> 01:16:36.916
Seriously,

1448
01:16:37.000 --> 01:16:38.476
she's going to be so mad
that you still have these.

1449
01:16:38.500 --> 01:16:39.708
She told us to burn them.

1450
01:16:39.791 --> 01:16:41.333
I know. That's why I kept them.

1451
01:16:41.416 --> 01:16:43.684
We've been talking about, like,
really serious stuff, though.

1452
01:16:43.708 --> 01:16:45.333
Like future stuff?

1453
01:16:45.416 --> 01:16:48.166
Like serious stuff, like…

1454
01:16:48.250 --> 01:16:50.250
Where we would want to live.

1455
01:16:50.333 --> 01:16:51.625
Oh, my God.

1456
01:16:51.708 --> 01:16:53.500
Do you think he'll propose?

1457
01:16:53.583 --> 01:16:55.166
- Would you say yes?
- Uh...

1458
01:16:55.250 --> 01:16:57.083
Well, yeah, I'd say yes.

1459
01:16:57.166 --> 01:16:59.583
But...

1460
01:17:01.291 --> 01:17:03.041
I think I'm confused.

1461
01:17:03.125 --> 01:17:05.208
Yeah, what you confused about?

1462
01:17:05.291 --> 01:17:10.041
I have always found comfort

1463
01:17:10.125 --> 01:17:12.583
in... the plan.

1464
01:17:12.666 --> 01:17:14.291
- And...
- What plan?

1465
01:17:14.375 --> 01:17:15.875
The, uh...

1466
01:17:15.958 --> 01:17:19.416
The plan, like, my plan,
how things are supposed to go.

1467
01:17:19.500 --> 01:17:22.416
Uh, there... there's always a,
there's a formula.

1468
01:17:22.500 --> 01:17:26.083
And it is go to school,
get the degree, get the job,

1469
01:17:26.166 --> 01:17:28.875
eventually meet someone,
and then that equals fulfillment.

1470
01:17:28.958 --> 01:17:30.666
And I'm grateful for it, I am,

1471
01:17:30.750 --> 01:17:32.125
but I...

1472
01:17:32.208 --> 01:17:34.791
I...

1473
01:17:34.875 --> 01:17:39.416
I don't know if I want New York anymore.

1474
01:17:39.500 --> 01:17:42.000
And I don't know
if I want this job anymore.

1475
01:17:42.083 --> 01:17:44.041
Well, shit, that's a big decision.

1476
01:17:44.125 --> 01:17:45.500
I know.

1477
01:17:46.958 --> 01:17:49.458
Well, then why are you doing it
if you don't want it?

1478
01:17:49.541 --> 01:17:51.208
Because I don't...

1479
01:17:51.291 --> 01:17:54.583
I don't wa... want to
disappoint you, and...

1480
01:17:54.666 --> 01:17:57.250
You can't disappoint me.

1481
01:17:57.333 --> 01:17:58.642
The only way you could disappoint me

1482
01:17:58.666 --> 01:18:00.708
is if you did something
you didn't want to do.

1483
01:18:00.791 --> 01:18:03.833
I never quite understood
why you wanted to work in a bank.

1484
01:18:03.916 --> 01:18:05.916
I get it, the money, but...

1485
01:18:06.000 --> 01:18:09.750
Baby, you got to do what you love
or-or at least something you like.

1486
01:18:09.833 --> 01:18:12.583
I don't think I'd love it or like it.

1487
01:18:12.666 --> 01:18:14.666
Well, who would?

1488
01:18:14.750 --> 01:18:16.125
I get it.

1489
01:18:16.208 --> 01:18:18.166
Hey, you're young.

1490
01:18:18.250 --> 01:18:21.416
You got a whole life to make
some sort of decisions like that.

1491
01:18:21.500 --> 01:18:22.666
I think that's the thing.

1492
01:18:22.750 --> 01:18:26.291
I think that's the first time
I've been asking myself that question.

1493
01:18:26.375 --> 01:18:30.250
And I think when I was with him,
I think that...

1494
01:18:30.333 --> 01:18:33.500
like, I wasn't... I wasn't thinking
about expectations of myself.

1495
01:18:33.583 --> 01:18:36.041
I wasn't thinking about
where I needed to go,

1496
01:18:36.125 --> 01:18:40.000
who I needed to be,
what I needed to be do... uh, doing.

1497
01:18:40.083 --> 01:18:42.666
I was just there with him.

1498
01:18:42.750 --> 01:18:45.125
Yeah, it's called freedom. You felt free.

1499
01:18:45.208 --> 01:18:47.000
Yeah, and I'm missing that.

1500
01:18:47.083 --> 01:18:48.541
Baby, you'll find that again.

1501
01:18:48.625 --> 01:18:50.309
I mean, I don't think you're going
to find it in a bank, though,

1502
01:18:50.333 --> 01:18:52.208
that's for sure.

1503
01:18:53.375 --> 01:18:58.375
I'm not trying to say you didn't have
an amazing experience with him.

1504
01:18:58.458 --> 01:19:00.000
I'm actually saying the opposite.

1505
01:19:00.083 --> 01:19:01.833
He gave you something.

1506
01:19:01.916 --> 01:19:05.000
He gave you something to strive for.

1507
01:19:05.083 --> 01:19:07.583
- A feeling to strive for.
- Mm-hmm.

1508
01:19:08.208 --> 01:19:10.166
I think so, too.

1509
01:19:10.250 --> 01:19:12.916
Well, that's a big, big gift.

1510
01:19:13.750 --> 01:19:15.250
- I love you.
- I love you, too.

1511
01:19:15.333 --> 01:19:17.000
It's good to be home.

1512
01:21:00.458 --> 01:21:01.833
Heather?

1513
01:21:01.916 --> 01:21:03.583
- Hi.
- Hi. Have you seen my shoes?

1514
01:21:03.666 --> 01:21:05.791
Um, yeah, right there.

1515
01:21:05.875 --> 01:21:07.291
Oh.

1516
01:21:08.583 --> 01:21:10.708
Okay, you need to hurry up. She's waiting.

1517
01:21:10.791 --> 01:21:12.708
- Come on.
- Okay.

1518
01:21:33.541 --> 01:21:35.583
I declare you husband and wife.

1519
01:21:41.875 --> 01:21:43.083
Whoo!

1520
01:21:55.625 --> 01:21:57.166
You got the best girl.

1521
01:21:57.958 --> 01:21:59.333
Yeah, I do know that.

1522
01:21:59.416 --> 01:22:00.833
In the world.

1523
01:22:03.958 --> 01:22:06.041
So, nothing?

1524
01:22:06.125 --> 01:22:07.958
Not a word?

1525
01:22:11.708 --> 01:22:13.333
You know?

1526
01:22:14.666 --> 01:22:16.250
Come with me.

1527
01:22:17.750 --> 01:22:19.291
Okay.

1528
01:22:19.375 --> 01:22:21.791
He never RSVP'd.

1529
01:22:21.875 --> 01:22:24.208
He just sent me a wedding gift.

1530
01:22:25.500 --> 01:22:26.750
And this.

1531
01:22:27.958 --> 01:22:29.541
It's for you.

1532
01:22:29.625 --> 01:22:31.750
I haven't read it. Don't worry.

1533
01:22:31.833 --> 01:22:33.666
Uh, and Connie doesn't know about it.

1534
01:22:33.750 --> 01:22:37.166
But he only said to give it to you
if you really asked about him.

1535
01:22:37.250 --> 01:22:38.541
So...

1536
01:22:40.875 --> 01:22:42.208
- Okay.
- Um...

1537
01:22:42.291 --> 01:22:43.767
but I'll be out there if you need me.

1538
01:22:43.791 --> 01:22:45.125
Okay.

1539
01:22:52.958 --> 01:22:55.125
Heather...

1540
01:22:55.208 --> 01:22:58.666
I know vanishing at the airport
was an unforgivable thing to do.

1541
01:23:00.666 --> 01:23:03.706
Watching you board the plane alone
was the hardest thing that I've ever done.

1542
01:23:06.666 --> 01:23:09.666
But at that moment,
I felt I had no choice.

1543
01:23:17.166 --> 01:23:18.791
I lied to you.

1544
01:23:18.875 --> 01:23:20.791
About how sick I'd been before.

1545
01:23:20.875 --> 01:23:23.333
How scared I was
the cancer would come back.

1546
01:23:24.333 --> 01:23:25.916
And suddenly there it was.

1547
01:23:26.000 --> 01:23:28.541
In an instant, my future was uncertain.

1548
01:23:29.916 --> 01:23:32.541
There was one thing that I knew for sure.

1549
01:23:32.625 --> 01:23:35.125
I couldn't ask you to watch me die.

1550
01:23:35.208 --> 01:23:36.375
I had to leave.

1551
01:23:36.458 --> 01:23:39.541
I had to hope
that you'd hate me for doing it,

1552
01:23:39.625 --> 01:23:43.000
that you'd move on
and find the happiness that you deserve.

1553
01:23:44.666 --> 01:23:46.458
I miss you.

1554
01:23:46.541 --> 01:23:49.541
I only think of you more and more
as the months go by.

1555
01:23:49.625 --> 01:23:53.500
The two weeks we spent together
have become my favorite movie in my head.

1556
01:23:54.583 --> 01:23:58.250
I play it over and over again,
hoping the memories never fade.

1557
01:24:00.708 --> 01:24:05.625
All my travels, my philosophizing,
all my grand ideas.

1558
01:24:05.708 --> 01:24:08.583
What I know now is that I wasn't
following the journal.

1559
01:24:08.666 --> 01:24:10.541
I was running from the truth.

1560
01:24:11.916 --> 01:24:16.750
The journal wasn't some self-help book
or guide to find fulfillment.

1561
01:24:16.833 --> 01:24:18.833
It was a map...

1562
01:24:18.916 --> 01:24:21.250
that led me to you.

1563
01:24:21.333 --> 01:24:25.625
I still keep it with me,
but I read it differently now.

1564
01:24:26.916 --> 01:24:30.041
Finding you made every bit
of that journey worthwhile.

1565
01:24:31.291 --> 01:24:35.000
It has given me strength
to face whatever comes next.

1566
01:24:36.500 --> 01:24:40.625
Love is what makes us dance
in the face of death.

1567
01:24:45.250 --> 01:24:47.333
"They are dancing
in the face of death."

1568
01:24:48.166 --> 01:24:49.833
Don't know when they'll stop.

1569
01:24:49.916 --> 01:24:51.916
"Maybe I won't, either."

1570
01:25:02.166 --> 01:25:05.000
♪ In the darkness ♪

1571
01:25:05.083 --> 01:25:09.541
♪ I was struggling the hardest ♪

1572
01:25:09.625 --> 01:25:14.583
♪ I've been going, going on my own ♪

1573
01:25:14.666 --> 01:25:16.041
I think I need to go.

1574
01:25:16.125 --> 01:25:17.500
Wait, you think he's there?

1575
01:25:17.583 --> 01:25:18.708
I don't know.

1576
01:25:21.416 --> 01:25:23.291
But I need to go.

1577
01:25:23.375 --> 01:25:25.166
I have to have hope.

1578
01:25:26.250 --> 01:25:28.583
I don't know. I don't know.

1579
01:25:28.666 --> 01:25:30.346
- I love you.
- I love you so much.

1580
01:25:30.416 --> 01:25:31.656
- I love you.
- Congratulations.

1581
01:25:31.708 --> 01:25:32.875
Thank you.

1582
01:25:32.958 --> 01:25:33.958
Okay, go.

1583
01:25:34.041 --> 01:25:35.708
Honey, you need to go.

1584
01:25:35.791 --> 01:25:37.583
You need to go right now.

1585
01:25:53.208 --> 01:25:56.333
- ♪ I will find you ♪
- ♪ I will find you ♪

1586
01:27:13.750 --> 01:27:15.291
Hi.

1587
01:27:19.375 --> 01:27:21.166
How'd you find me?

1588
01:27:21.250 --> 01:27:25.250
I remembered the festival,
"dancing in the face of death."

1589
01:27:27.125 --> 01:27:28.833
Heather, I can't offer you... I don't...

1590
01:27:28.916 --> 01:27:31.166
I can't... I can't...
I can't give you a future.

1591
01:27:31.250 --> 01:27:33.500
I don't need you to.

1592
01:27:34.500 --> 01:27:36.458
Do you remember what you told me?

1593
01:27:38.250 --> 01:27:41.416
If you think it, it's yours.

1594
01:27:44.416 --> 01:27:47.041
I'm here now, and I love you.

1595
01:27:50.291 --> 01:27:52.625
And I want to dance.

1596
01:27:54.041 --> 01:27:55.875
I love you, too.

1597
01:28:04.208 --> 01:28:06.250
♪ I see you ♪

1598
01:28:06.333 --> 01:28:10.500
- ♪ Close my eyes and I can feel you ♪
- ♪ Close my eyes and I can feel you ♪

1599
